WEBVTT

00:01:31.630 --> 00:01:36.400
CLOCK HILL TENNIS CLUB

00:01:37.010 --> 00:01:39.260
Coach Mitaka's finally getting
married tomorrow.

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:39.960
Yes.

00:01:46.450 --> 00:01:47.430
What's going on?

00:01:47.590 --> 00:01:48.300
Signing.

00:01:48.490 --> 00:01:49.380
Signing what?

00:01:49.510 --> 00:01:51.740
Tomorrow is
Coach Mitaka's wedding,

00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:56.180
so we decided to send him
a racket with our messages on it.

00:01:56.460 --> 00:01:57.850
Would you two like
to write a note?

00:01:57.990 --> 00:02:00.850
Sure! You go first, Manager.

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:02.880
Then here.
Now you probably.

00:02:02.990 --> 00:02:05.990
have a thing or two to
say to Coach, don't you?

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:06.950
well...

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:10.200
Not really.

00:02:10.670 --> 00:02:16.910
How about a gripe, like,
"How dare you dump me?"

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:21.390
Why can't you just be happy
for those who find happiness?

00:02:30.030 --> 00:02:40.820
"I wish you a lifetime
of happiness. -- Kyoko Otonashi"

00:03:44.330 --> 00:03:49.850
Let us all raise our glasses
to wish Coach Mitaka happiness!

00:03:49.980 --> 00:03:51.440
Cheers!

00:03:53.310 --> 00:03:55.730
I heard the reception
is at the Imperia Hotel.

00:03:56.410 --> 00:03:58.380
I would have loved to partake
in French cuisine

00:03:58.450 --> 00:03:59.570
at an exclusive hotel.

00:03:59.750 --> 00:04:02.760
For their honeymoon, they're
going on a Mediterranean cruise

00:04:02.850 --> 00:04:05.350
from Greece to Spain.

00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:08.820
Manager sure missed
her chance.

00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:09.670
Yeah.

00:04:10.420 --> 00:04:12.980
I don't know what cruel fate
made her choose this one.

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:14.350
Leave me alone.

00:04:14.700 --> 00:04:16.450
Where is the manager, anyway?

00:04:16.530 --> 00:04:18.580
I think she's cooking.

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:21.860
We'll have to make do with
her homemade cooking.

00:04:22.260 --> 00:04:24.380
If you don't want it,
don't eat it.

00:04:24.470 --> 00:04:27.070
You didn't hear it,
because I didn't say it!

00:04:27.180 --> 00:04:31.310
By the way, Godai,
how far have you two gone?

00:04:32.920 --> 00:04:36.010
W-We. uh.

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:38.250
I'm not asking about that.

00:04:38.710 --> 00:04:39.700
You know, have you
set the date

00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:41.400
for the engagement ceremony
or the wedding?

00:04:41.690 --> 00:04:43.510
You've made some
sort of plans, right?

00:04:43.860 --> 00:04:46.320
N-No, nothing like that.

00:04:46.890 --> 00:04:50.130
But I heard you got
the manager's parents' blessing.

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:51.320
We did.

00:04:51.390 --> 00:04:56.650
Then it's your turn to take
Manager to meet your folks.

00:04:57.770 --> 00:04:59.800
Get with the program.

00:04:59.880 --> 00:05:04.010
You better pick up the pace before
Manager changes her mind.

00:05:09.380 --> 00:05:11.050
Yes? Come in.

00:05:12.510 --> 00:05:14.950
I was just about to
take everything upstairs.

00:05:19.060 --> 00:05:19.640
Um..

00:05:19.720 --> 00:05:20.200
Yes?

00:05:22.130 --> 00:05:25.880
Would you mind coming with me
to Niigata in the near future?

00:05:27.400 --> 00:05:28.800
I want you to
see my grandma

00:05:28.870 --> 00:05:30.630
and meet my parents
as my fiancée.

00:05:32.110 --> 00:05:32.630
Sure.

00:05:33.880 --> 00:05:34.930
Y-You will?!

00:05:35.950 --> 00:05:36.380
Yes.

00:05:36.820 --> 00:05:38.810
I'll call them now.

00:05:46.260 --> 00:05:49.010
GODAI

00:05:49.450 --> 00:05:54.920
You're getting married?!
Great! Good for you, Yusaku!

00:05:55.870 --> 00:05:58.320
So I want to take
some time off and.

00:06:00.330 --> 00:06:03.930
Then come right away.
You get here tomorrow.

00:06:04.310 --> 00:06:04.930
Wha--?!

00:06:05.380 --> 00:06:06.760
T-Tomorrow?!

00:06:07.110 --> 00:06:10.330
I'm sorry.
You know how self-serving she is.

00:06:11.070 --> 00:06:13.130
But we don't have
to go tomorrow.

00:06:13.690 --> 00:06:15.680
You must have plans.

00:06:16.380 --> 00:06:18.510
I can go any time.

00:06:19.780 --> 00:06:24.140
I have to go sooner
or later anyway.

00:06:24.450 --> 00:06:25.820
K-Kyoko!

00:06:26.590 --> 00:06:28.080
Banzai!

00:06:28.430 --> 00:06:29.880
We heard!

00:06:29.960 --> 00:06:31.430
Well done!

00:06:31.500 --> 00:06:33.210
What're you all doing?!

00:06:34.030 --> 00:06:36.960
You were taking so long,
we came down to see what's up.

00:06:37.030 --> 00:06:39.080
That's great, Godai!

00:06:39.180 --> 00:06:41.630
It took long enough for
spring to arrive at your door.

00:06:41.900 --> 00:06:46.390
All right then! Tonight, we have
to celebrate their trip to Niigata!

00:06:46.490 --> 00:06:48.340
Let's party!

00:07:01.170 --> 00:07:03.130
Is this too much makeup?

00:07:03.330 --> 00:07:04.380
No.

00:07:15.110 --> 00:07:17.220
This dress isn't
too flashy, is it?

00:07:17.770 --> 00:07:18.940
No.

00:07:24.060 --> 00:07:25.510
Do you think this one's better?

00:07:26.780 --> 00:07:27.710
It's fine.

00:07:36.870 --> 00:07:39.060
We'll be going.

00:07:39.460 --> 00:07:40.990
Leave everything to us.

00:07:41.170 --> 00:07:42.710
Don't you worry
about a thing.

00:07:43.070 --> 00:07:44.830
Say hello to Grandma.

00:07:45.200 --> 00:07:45.860
Bye.

00:07:49.340 --> 00:07:50.890
See you, Soichiro.

00:07:52.570 --> 00:07:56.880
I hope she'll be all right.
She seems pretty nervous.

00:07:56.990 --> 00:08:00.440
Can't help it. She's older,
and it's her second marriage.

00:08:01.060 --> 00:08:02.320
Godai may be fine with that,

00:08:02.380 --> 00:08:04.510
but who knows how
his parents will take it.

00:08:04.720 --> 00:08:08.180
Country folks tend to be more
picky about things like that.

00:08:08.430 --> 00:08:10.620
I think everything
will be fine.

00:08:10.960 --> 00:08:13.150
If he'd taken
Akemi home, though...

00:08:13.240 --> 00:08:15.460
that would have been
different story.

00:08:27.140 --> 00:08:28.170
What's the matter?

00:08:28.450 --> 00:08:30.240
I'm kind of nervous.

00:08:32.110 --> 00:08:36.840
Do your parents know
everything about me?

00:08:38.320 --> 00:08:39.290
You know...

00:08:40.070 --> 00:08:41.580
Do they know how old I am?

00:08:42.430 --> 00:08:46.080
And that this is
my second time?

00:08:50.280 --> 00:08:52.860
Don't worry.
They'll love you.

00:08:59.610 --> 00:09:00.870
Hello?

00:09:02.690 --> 00:09:04.370
Grandma!

00:09:05.710 --> 00:09:08.610
Godai and Kyoko?
They left a while ago.

00:09:10.750 --> 00:09:13.690
Huh? Sure.

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:16.660
Of course!

00:09:17.900 --> 00:09:21.520
All right. Bye.

00:09:23.140 --> 00:09:24.350
Who was that?

00:09:24.910 --> 00:09:26.700
Godai's grandma.

00:09:45.300 --> 00:09:46.480
Are you warm enough?

00:09:46.700 --> 00:09:47.420
Yes.

00:09:49.120 --> 00:09:52.570
Grandma said she'd
be here to pick us up.

00:09:56.070 --> 00:09:57.820
W-What are you doing?!

00:09:58.540 --> 00:10:00.700
Grandma. You seem well

00:10:01.070 --> 00:10:04.040
It's been a while, Manager!

00:10:04.870 --> 00:10:07.700
Or may I call you Kyoko?

00:10:08.020 --> 00:10:09.840
I'm so glad you've come.

00:10:10.710 --> 00:10:11.500
Grandma.

00:10:23.730 --> 00:10:26.350
We're almost there, Kyoko.

00:10:26.600 --> 00:10:27.160
Yes.

00:10:41.110 --> 00:10:44.680
This is where Yusaku grew up.

00:10:49.700 --> 00:10:51.850
Come in and make
yourself at home.

00:10:51.930 --> 00:10:52.550
Yes.

00:10:53.900 --> 00:10:56.080
OPEN

00:10:56.490 --> 00:10:57.210
Welco--!

00:10:57.960 --> 00:10:59.450
Dad, it's Yusaku!

00:11:00.730 --> 00:11:01.450
You're home!

00:11:01.810 --> 00:11:03.400
Why did you open up shop?

00:11:03.680 --> 00:11:06.570
Kyoko came all
the way here to see you.

00:11:06.810 --> 00:11:09.460
Godai, it's okay.

00:11:09.650 --> 00:11:12.050
Thank you for coming so far.

00:11:12.840 --> 00:11:15.040
We've heard the great news.

00:11:15.190 --> 00:11:17.950
It's very nice to meet you.
I'm Kyoko Otonashi

00:11:18.820 --> 00:11:19.780
You know..

00:11:19.890 --> 00:11:20.910
Welcome home.

00:11:21.160 --> 00:11:22.370
Don't "welcome home" me.

00:11:22.450 --> 00:11:24.320
How could you be open on
an important day like this?

00:11:24.530 --> 00:11:29.110
We were planning to
close for the day.

00:11:29.200 --> 00:11:31.820
but Grandma insisted
that we stay open.

00:11:32.040 --> 00:11:34.320
Grandma?! Why?!

00:11:34.730 --> 00:11:39.200
Why not? Kyoko's going
to be joining our family.

00:11:39.280 --> 00:11:42.230
There's no need to be
so formal, right?

00:11:42.370 --> 00:11:43.140
Right.

00:11:43.470 --> 00:11:44.120
Yes.

00:11:46.650 --> 00:11:49.730
I'm sorry I won't be able
to treat you like a guest.

00:11:50.290 --> 00:11:51.780
Please don't.

00:11:52.350 --> 00:11:53.570
Pork cutlet bowl pickup!

00:11:54.060 --> 00:11:54.840
Okay!

00:11:55.820 --> 00:11:57.980
I'm sorry it's
rather unsettling.

00:11:58.560 --> 00:11:59.450
Please, it's all right.

00:12:03.400 --> 00:12:06.750
We're so glad
that you've come.

00:12:06.830 --> 00:12:07.700
Thank you.

00:12:09.410 --> 00:12:11.450
Ordering two tempura bowls!

00:12:11.780 --> 00:12:13.170
Okay!

00:12:14.410 --> 00:12:17.170
May I help you
at the restaurant?

00:12:17.240 --> 00:12:17.800
What?!

00:12:18.210 --> 00:12:19.940
I can't impose on you
to do that

00:12:20.080 --> 00:12:22.480
Sure. Let her help you.

00:12:22.550 --> 00:12:23.410
Grandma!

00:12:23.480 --> 00:12:24.240
What?

00:12:24.610 --> 00:12:27.570
I'd rather keep myself busy.

00:12:27.690 --> 00:12:28.470
But.

00:12:28.560 --> 00:12:29.650
Thank you.

00:12:29.720 --> 00:12:30.480
No problem.

00:12:30.750 --> 00:12:31.690
Kyoko!

00:12:32.090 --> 00:12:33.290
Let her be.

00:12:33.770 --> 00:12:35.390
But Yusaku.

00:12:36.090 --> 00:12:38.320
I have something
important to talk to you about.

00:12:39.270 --> 00:12:39.790
Huh?

00:12:55.610 --> 00:12:57.330
What's so important?

00:12:57.840 --> 00:13:01.200
Yusaku, do you have money
saved up for your wedding?

00:13:02.250 --> 00:13:04.580
What made you bring that up?

00:13:05.140 --> 00:13:06.840
You got it or not?!

00:13:07.720 --> 00:13:11.210
I just got a job.
I'll start saving.

00:13:11.620 --> 00:13:13.740
So you're planning
to make Kyoko wait

00:13:13.820 --> 00:13:14.710
until you have enough?

00:13:16.830 --> 00:13:18.120
Use this.

00:13:21.360 --> 00:13:23.010
But it's your-

00:13:23.520 --> 00:13:24.880
Go ahead and use it.

00:13:25.200 --> 00:13:27.360
I'll have to live to be 10O

00:13:27.440 --> 00:13:29.460
if I have to wait until
you save up enough.

00:13:31.530 --> 00:13:33.830
But I can't accept this much.

00:13:33.980 --> 00:13:35.570
I'm not giving it to you!

00:13:36.710 --> 00:13:40.630
I was saving that
for my funeral.

00:13:41.370 --> 00:13:42.600
So you better pay me back
before I die.

00:13:45.490 --> 00:13:46.320
Grandma!

00:13:47.750 --> 00:13:49.770
I'll make sure you have
a great funeral!

00:13:51.230 --> 00:13:53.410
Can't you think of
a nicer way to thank me?

00:13:55.230 --> 00:13:56.510
Welcome!

00:13:59.340 --> 00:14:00.100
Please.

00:14:01.630 --> 00:14:03.290
You hired new help?

00:14:03.400 --> 00:14:05.890
No, she's going to
be Yusaku's bride.

00:14:06.110 --> 00:14:07.230
My name is Kyoko.

00:14:07.440 --> 00:14:09.600
What a beauty.

00:14:09.950 --> 00:14:11.370
Pleased to meet you.

00:14:12.720 --> 00:14:13.840
Welcome!

00:14:15.120 --> 00:14:16.870
This way, we won't have to
go around the neighborhood

00:14:16.950 --> 00:14:18.000
to introduce you.

00:14:18.960 --> 00:14:20.140
Grandma had a great idea.

00:14:21.960 --> 00:14:23.350
Pork cutlet bowl
and curry udon.

00:14:23.650 --> 00:14:26.620
Ordering pork cutlet bowl
and curry udon!

00:14:26.790 --> 00:14:27.550
Gotcha!

00:14:27.830 --> 00:14:29.620
What are you doing, Yusaku?

00:14:29.830 --> 00:14:30.990
Nothing.

00:14:31.070 --> 00:14:32.650
Looks like you
need something to do.

00:14:35.130 --> 00:14:36.600
Geez!

00:14:37.470 --> 00:14:40.390
I didn't come home
to do this.

00:14:42.130 --> 00:14:43.390
Good evening!

00:14:43.480 --> 00:14:45.200
Here you are!

00:14:46.320 --> 00:14:47.670
We're here to
see the bride.

00:14:47.750 --> 00:14:48.900
Kyoko!

00:14:49.040 --> 00:14:49.840
Yes?!

00:14:55.360 --> 00:14:57.320
This is Yusaku's bride.

00:14:57.750 --> 00:14:59.720
N-Nice to meet you.

00:15:00.460 --> 00:15:02.170
What a beauty.

00:15:02.370 --> 00:15:04.730
She looks like a doll

00:15:05.330 --> 00:15:08.690
Everything's on me tonight!
Don't hold back!

00:15:24.590 --> 00:15:25.570
What's going on?!

00:15:25.650 --> 00:15:27.010
I'm introducing the bride.

00:15:27.120 --> 00:15:29.110
I'm so happy for you, Yu-chan.

00:15:29.250 --> 00:15:31.010
You're a lucky man.

00:15:31.090 --> 00:15:32.010
Thank you.

00:15:33.420 --> 00:15:35.220
Sorry, Kyoko.

00:15:35.600 --> 00:15:36.580
No problem.

00:15:38.890 --> 00:15:42.650
Another delivery, Yusaku.
Murano residence on Third.

00:15:42.740 --> 00:15:44.160
Two tempura soba.

00:15:44.870 --> 00:15:47.600
Can you treat Kyoko
more kindly?

00:15:47.710 --> 00:15:50.160
We intended to.

00:15:50.370 --> 00:15:52.970
But you better let
Grandma have her way.

00:15:53.540 --> 00:15:56.570
You never know how much
longer she'll be with us.

00:15:57.090 --> 00:15:59.080
Not that again.

00:16:00.690 --> 00:16:02.770
I'm so happy for you.

00:16:02.860 --> 00:16:06.410
Coming so far to this
little rural town.

00:16:06.790 --> 00:16:08.620
That's for sure!

00:16:09.600 --> 00:16:13.540
WE ARE CLOSED

00:16:15.570 --> 00:16:16.520
Where's Kyoko?

00:16:17.370 --> 00:16:19.600
She went upstairs
with Grandma.

00:16:20.030 --> 00:16:21.050
Upstairs?

00:16:21.210 --> 00:16:24.330
We'll close up shop.
Go ahead.

00:16:24.900 --> 00:16:25.700
Okay.

00:16:29.280 --> 00:16:33.240
This is a ring that Grandpa
gave me when we were young.

00:16:33.550 --> 00:16:37.040
It's nothing expensive,
but I want you to have it.

00:16:37.330 --> 00:16:40.990
I can't accept such
a precious memento.

00:16:41.420 --> 00:16:43.330
I just can't.

00:16:44.500 --> 00:16:45.460
What's going on?

00:16:45.570 --> 00:16:47.090
You get out of here!

00:16:47.890 --> 00:16:48.510
Why?

00:16:48.600 --> 00:16:50.960
Just get out!

00:16:59.950 --> 00:17:01.630
I always intended
to give this ring

00:17:01.720 --> 00:17:04.710
to the woman Yusaku would
choose as his bride.

00:17:07.310 --> 00:17:11.680
Please accept this
to remember me by.

00:17:12.550 --> 00:17:15.010
Grandma, please don't say that.

00:17:15.400 --> 00:17:17.630
I raised Yusaku.

00:17:18.200 --> 00:17:20.490
He may be a little
absent-minded and unreliable,

00:17:20.670 --> 00:17:21.850
but I think I did my best

00:17:21.940 --> 00:17:23.660
to raise him
to be a good person.

00:17:24.210 --> 00:17:26.760
I'm so pleased that
you'll be his wife.

00:17:28.800 --> 00:17:30.000
The pleasure is mine.

00:17:32.250 --> 00:17:33.680
Thank you so much.

00:17:36.490 --> 00:17:39.250
So you'll accept this ring?

00:17:41.580 --> 00:17:43.270
Yes, with gratitude.

00:17:48.320 --> 00:17:50.310
Yusaku! Yusaku!

00:17:51.970 --> 00:17:54.250
First, you kick me out,
and now you want me in here?

00:17:54.330 --> 00:17:55.090
Sit.

00:17:59.240 --> 00:18:01.350
Put this on Kyoko's finger.

00:18:01.710 --> 00:18:02.250
What?

00:18:03.910 --> 00:18:05.200
Where did you get this?

00:18:05.500 --> 00:18:06.760
Just shut up and do it.

00:18:43.490 --> 00:18:46.220
I feel so relieved now...

00:18:49.130 --> 00:18:49.840
Grandma?

00:18:51.960 --> 00:18:52.810
Grandma?

00:18:52.900 --> 00:18:53.750
Grandma?

00:18:56.900 --> 00:18:57.880
G-Grandma?

00:18:58.470 --> 00:18:59.400
Grandma?

00:19:00.060 --> 00:19:01.320
Hey! Grandma?!

00:19:02.140 --> 00:19:02.970
Grandma?

00:19:04.530 --> 00:19:05.750
- You can't be...
- Grandma!

00:19:06.070 --> 00:19:07.830
Grandma! Get a
hold of yourself!

00:19:07.940 --> 00:19:10.130
Grandma! Grandma!

00:19:10.710 --> 00:19:11.670
Grandma!

00:19:15.580 --> 00:19:16.680
Just kidding!

00:19:19.080 --> 00:19:21.510
I can't die until I hold
my great-grandchild.

00:19:21.720 --> 00:19:23.500
Besides, there's no more
money for my funeral.

00:19:24.780 --> 00:19:26.910
You sour prune!

00:19:33.760 --> 00:19:35.930
Thank you so much.

00:19:36.000 --> 00:19:38.050
You're so thoughtful

00:19:38.470 --> 00:19:40.080
I'm glad to help.

00:19:40.880 --> 00:19:43.100
Yusaku, what a wonderful
woman you've found.

00:19:43.680 --> 00:19:44.730
Thanks.

00:19:44.880 --> 00:19:49.330
We're very happy that
you'll be our son's bride.

00:19:49.720 --> 00:19:52.110
I'm very happy to be
a part of your family.

00:19:52.810 --> 00:19:54.530
Finally, this is starting
to feel more like it.

00:19:54.610 --> 00:19:56.540
What's the formality?

00:19:57.250 --> 00:20:00.250
We're going to have
a party tonight.

00:20:01.230 --> 00:20:04.920
Sure. Yusaku brought his bride
all the way here, after all

00:20:05.520 --> 00:20:07.490
I'll put together
something to eat

00:20:09.710 --> 00:20:10.820
- Here.
- Thanks.

00:20:13.180 --> 00:20:13.900
Please.

00:20:13.980 --> 00:20:14.800
Thanks.

00:20:22.270 --> 00:20:25.030
They're late.
What's taking them so long?

00:20:27.580 --> 00:20:28.950
Someone's here.

00:20:29.010 --> 00:20:30.530
Yusaku, go get the door.

00:20:31.960 --> 00:20:33.390
Geez.

00:20:35.200 --> 00:20:38.020
Coming! But we're closed for--

00:20:39.400 --> 00:20:42.130
Hey! Open up!

00:20:44.240 --> 00:20:47.500
More the merrier, right?

00:20:47.570 --> 00:20:50.480
Let's party tonight!

00:20:50.570 --> 00:20:53.360
We've heard that you're always
looking out for Yusaku.

00:20:53.540 --> 00:20:56.170
It must be fate.

00:20:56.270 --> 00:20:58.560
Bottoms up!

00:20:58.650 --> 00:20:59.800
Thank you.

00:21:00.510 --> 00:21:04.180
Smile, Godai and Manager.

00:21:04.730 --> 00:21:06.550
We'll drink all night
gazing at the snow

00:21:06.630 --> 00:21:08.890
to celebrate your
bright future!

00:21:19.030 --> 00:21:21.200
It's like we never
left the apartment.

00:21:21.440 --> 00:21:23.430
There's more sake here.

00:21:23.600 --> 00:21:25.290
Where's Kyoko?

00:21:25.950 --> 00:21:27.330
She's not here.

00:21:30.690 --> 00:21:32.040
Anthology of Japanese Literature

00:21:42.000 --> 00:21:44.750
Yusaku, for your 17th birthday

00:21:46.470 --> 00:21:48.130
Grandma gave those to me.

00:21:50.260 --> 00:21:51.630
I hardly read them.

00:21:52.530 --> 00:21:54.790
I'm sorry I came in here
without asking.

00:21:55.070 --> 00:21:58.200
It's okay. It's sort
of a dull room.

00:21:59.980 --> 00:22:01.020
Not at all

00:22:02.220 --> 00:22:04.830
This was your room?

00:22:05.190 --> 00:22:08.510
Yes, until I graduated
from high school.

00:22:09.510 --> 00:22:11.480
and moved to Maison Ikkoku.

00:22:11.850 --> 00:22:12.540
What's this?

00:22:24.560 --> 00:22:27.550
Those were my
rugby teammates.

00:22:28.910 --> 00:22:33.030
We're all smiling, but
that was after a huge loss.

00:22:34.450 --> 00:22:36.170
But it looks like
you had a great time.

00:22:53.360 --> 00:22:56.930
You grew up watching
this town, every day?

00:22:57.800 --> 00:22:58.520
Yes.

00:23:03.150 --> 00:23:04.130
So beautiful

00:23:17.930 --> 00:23:19.040
Manager?

00:23:19.460 --> 00:23:21.980
Godai, where are you?

00:23:24.000 --> 00:23:25.190
Here they are!

00:23:25.260 --> 00:23:27.230
W-What are you all doing?!

00:23:27.360 --> 00:23:29.260
What are you two doing?

00:23:29.560 --> 00:23:31.160
Let me see! Let me see, too!

00:23:31.240 --> 00:23:32.000
Grandma!

00:23:32.740 --> 00:23:37.140
Let's celebrate the beginning
of their life together!

00:23:50.100 --> 00:23:52.390
It's been a long two years.

00:23:52.580 --> 00:23:54.570
We've somehow come
to a closure.

00:23:54.640 --> 00:23:57.240
Let's toast to Godai
and Manager's happiness

00:23:57.320 --> 00:23:59.750
and to the good health of
Maison Ikkoku fans worldwide!

00:23:59.850 --> 00:24:01.070
Cheers!

00:24:01.290 --> 00:24:04.870
Next: As Long as There's Love!
Maison Ikkoku Forever!
